## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical understanding of ACID, MVCC, and isolation levels with a concrete SQL pattern.

## Key Concepts

- Row-level locking with SELECT FOR UPDATE
- Atomic transfers and overdraft prevention
- READ COMMITTED vs SERIALIZABLE behaviors
- MVCC visibility and serialization failures

## Code Example

```sql
BEGIN;
SELECT balance INTO v FROM accounts WHERE id=101 FOR UPDATE;
IF v >= 50 THEN
  UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance - 50 WHERE id=101;
  UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance + 50 WHERE id=202;
  COMMIT;
ELSE
  ROLLBACK;
END IF;
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test concurrency to ensure no overdraft occurs?
- What retry strategy would you apply under SERIALIZABLE?
